nd item 2 (safety inspection) do not address either symptom on their face.\n- **Not shown:** The estimate does not show what diagnosis, if any, led to items 3 or 4.\n\n## Labels\n| Line | Label | Reason (quoted) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Question this | \"30,000-mile service package — required.\" Scope check: routine maintenance that does not match either symptom, and presented as required. |\n| 2 | Question this | \"Safety inspection — recommended.\" Scope check: an inspection that does not match either symptom. |\n| 3 | Standard | \"Per TSB 21-045, reprogram transmission control module.\" The bulletin number is given and the work fits the shifting complaint. |\n| 4 | Standard | \"Water pump ... 165.00.\" Fits the coolant complaint. Part name and price are shown. |\n| 5 | Check | \"Core charge ... 45.00.\" Pattern: core charge not explained. The estimate does not say what is returned, when, or whether the charge is refundable. |\n| 6 | Check | \"Labor — 2.0 hr @ 120.00/hr.\" Pattern L-3: labor without a stated basis. The rate and hours are shown, but no operation is named, so the hours cannot be tied to items 3 or 4. |\n| 7 | Check | \"Note: work in item 3 authorized verbally by phone.\" Pattern: verbal authorization noted. No written authorization line appears on the estimate. |\n| 8 | Standard | \"Sales tax 7% ... 59.43.\" Stated rate, and the amount matches 7% of $849.00. |\n\n## Questions to ask\n1. **What does the $189 \"required\" package include, and what makes it required for these symptoms?** A good answer itemizes the services, ties any of them to the shifting or coolant complaint, or says plainly that the package is routine maintenance and can be declined.\n\n2. **Please send the text of TSB 21-045 and a written authorization for the reprogram.** A good answer names the bulletin, states which vehicles and conditions it applies to, explains what the scan or test showed, and provides a written work order or authorization line for the $145.\n\n3. **Is the $45 core charge refundable, and what do I need to return to get it back?** A good answer says which part is the core, what condition it must be in, the return deadline, and where the refund is recorded.\n\n4. **Which operations do the 2.0 labor hours cover?** A good answer lists each operation with its hours, for example the reprogram and the pump replacement, so the total can be matched to the work.\n\n5. **Is the safety inspection required to do the repair, and what does it check?** A good answer says whether the inspection is optional and separate from the repair, and says whether written findings will be provided if it is done.\n\n## Decision\nThis reading does not approve, decline, or recommend anything. Your decision is yours to make.\n\nWhatever you decide, keep the paperwork trail:\n- Photograph or scan this estimate before you sign or leave the shop.\n- Write down what was promised by phone, the date and time, and the name of the person you spoke with.\n- Ask for any written authorization or work order to be emailed or printed, and keep it with the estimate and the invoice.\n\n## Needs confirmation\n- [NOT SHOWN: validity date for this estimate]\n- [NOT SHOWN: written authorization line for item 3 or for the estimate as a whole]\n- [NOT SHOWN: operations covered by the 2.0 labor hours]\n- [NOT SHOWN: diagnosis or test results behind items 3 and 4]\n- [NOT SHOWN: core charge return terms]\n- [CONFIRM: whether the core charge is included in the tax base, as the arithmetic indicates]","refusal":null,"reasoning":null,"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":2964,"completion_tokens":4929,"total_tokens":7893,"cost":0.0027609,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.00